+# Operational hazard: edge WAF blocks MCP payloads quoting shell-command signatures
+
+**Discovered:** 2026-10-27, while filing the bridge-20261027 work-order series.
+
+## What happened
+A bridge submission failed twice with HTTP 403 while submissions immediately before and after it
+succeeded — ruling out rate limiting. The error body was the edge WAF "Blocked" HTML page (not a
+tower error): the request was rejected before the tower's own validation could return a
+structured error.
+
+## Root cause (bisected)
+Using harmless JSON-RPC probe requests with candidate strings embedded in params, the trigger
+bisected to a quoted CLI inline-command invocation pattern — the interpreter name followed by the
+dash-c execution flag inside backticks (the classic one-liner form). The edge WAF body rule flags
+it. The acceptance criteria of one work order quoted exactly that form, and the whole submission
+was rejected. Minimal triggering prefix measured: 17 characters.
+
+## Impact
+- Agent loops hit opaque 403s with no machine-readable reason (WAF HTML, not JSON-RPC error)
+- Silent asymmetry: some work orders "never arrive" from the agent's perspective
+- Compounds the tower self-capability problem (#1329): the advertised write surface fails unpredictably
+
+## Recommended fixes (smallest first)
+1. **Document** the constraint in bridge_guide contract (wafBodyFilterNotes): paraphrase shell
+   invocations in prose; never quote the interpreter-name + dash-c form in payloads.
+2. **Pre-validate** in the bridge intake: detect the pattern in taskId/summary/files and return a
+   structured rejection with a human hint so agents self-correct in one retry.
+3. **Edge allow-rule** (Render ticket): exempt the MCP endpoint path from command-injection body
+   scanning.
+
+## Reproduction artifacts
+- Probe + bisect scripts preserved in the filing agent's workspace
+- Bisect result: whole doc blocked; 1 of 33 lines triggered; minimal prefix 17 chars
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:control-tower` `area:infra` `ops-hazard`
